      "description": "A DEVKIT or debug-station bios, dumped from a PlayStation 2 development unit. It boots like a retail one and tells a game it is a development machine, which some check. This project asks for Japan v2.50 (2010-04-15), which is the dump usually called ps2-0250j-20100415.bin. Another dump of the same release will do; a different release is a different machine, and the Boot ROM setting is where to say so.",
      "size": 4194304,
      "name": "ps2-0250j-20100415.bin",
      "sha1": "4B5EF16B67E3B523D28ED2406106CB80470A06D0",
      "label": "Japan v2.50 (2010-04-15)",
      "requiredWhen": {
        "setting": "bios",
        "is": "ps2-0250j-20100415"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "bios.bin",
      "display": "PlayStation 2 BIOS",
      "description": "The DVD PLAYER's own firmware, not a boot rom - a machine will not start from one. It is here because the choice is offered for completeness; if the machine does not boot, this is why. This project asks for DVD player USA v1.10, which is the dump usually called ps2-dvd-110u.bin. Another dump of the same release will do; a different release is a different machine, and the Boot ROM setting is where to say so.",
      "size": 2097152,
